# Skip onnxruntime-node's postinstall download.
#
# The CPU runtime we actually use (libonnxruntime.so.1 + onnxruntime_binding.node)
# ships inside the npm tarball. The postinstall exists only to fetch the CUDA 12
# and TensorRT execution-provider libraries from NuGet, which this app never
# loads — inference runs with executionProviders: ["cpu"], and no serverless
# host we deploy to has a GPU.
#
# Skipping it matters for three reasons:
#   1. The deploy stops depending on a NuGet CDN being reachable at build time.
#   2. Builds are faster and reproducible.
#   3. Vercel caps an unzipped serverless function at 250 MB. libonnxruntime.so.1
#      is already ~44 MB; adding the CUDA providers on top risks blowing that cap
#      and failing the deploy outright.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
